{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass</b> — Moses <b>on the road at the lodging-place</b>:" "<b>And He sought to kill him.</b> The angel (sought to kill) Moses: because he did not circumcise Eliezer his son, and for having been neglectful he was punished with death. It is taught — Rabbi Yosi said: Heaven forbid that he was neglectful; rather, he said: I shall circumcise and go on the road — it is dangerous for the infant for three days. I shall circumcise and wait three days. The Holy One, blessed be He, commanded me: Go, return to Egypt — so why was he punished? Because he occupied himself with the lodging first (Mekhilta). In tractate Nedarim: and the angel would make itself like a serpent and swallow him from his head to his thighs, and go back and swallow him from his feet to that same place. Zipporah understood that it was on account of the circumcision (Nedarim 32)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:35.050028740Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}